{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790012626,"nonce":"kdTN9JR4ZUqBZDZ84GwNMroiohI=","title":"gen-modsconfig.py ignores modDependencies/loadAfter, so dependents load before their dependencies","message":"profile/gen-modsconfig.py orders mods as LOAD_ORDER_HEAD, then the rest sorted by lowercased packageId, then LOAD_ORDER_TAIL. It reads modDependencies and loadAfter only to strip them while finding each mod's own packageId, and never uses them for ordering. So any mod outside the hard-coded lists loads in alphabetical order, whatever it depends on.\n\n**Seen on 2026-09-21:** linking Languages, FactionLanguages, ProgressionEducation and VanillaExpandedFramework produced dorian.languages BEFORE ferny.progressioneducation (a hard modDependency), and oskarpotocki.vanillafactionsexpanded.core AFTER ferny.progressioneducation (PE's hard dependency). Every run needed a hand-edited ModsConfig.xml plus run-agent.sh --no-modsconfig. A second session testing PrisonStandards has to do the same.\n\n**Fix:** after the head list, topologically order the remaining discovered mods by modDependencies, loadAfter and loadBefore (restricted to mods present), breaking ties alphabetically so the order stays deterministic. Keep the head/tail pins as they are.\n\n**Acceptance**\n\n1. With those four linked: VEF \u003c PE \u003c dorian.languages, with no hand edit.\n2. The existing 33-mod bench order is unchanged, or any change is explained.","files":null}]}